Current city model: events.city is a canonical slug, formerly constrained to NYC/Boston; public_events is anonymous discovery source. Profile and settings city checks also limited the vocabulary.
Metro strategy: Locally authored small metros reference table and public_active_metros projection. Registered metros with no approved upcoming events stay out of discovery. Foreign keys keep existing city slugs as the event join key.
New metros table required: NOT VERIFIED by the required production audit; migration remains local and must not be applied until audit and local database verification.
Reason: Current slugs have no stored centroid, name, or extensible vocabulary; production data might change the appropriate grouping strategy.
Active-metro query: public_active_metros groups public_events by metro slug with count and next date, filtered by event_date >= now(). Browser uses the normal Supabase client.
Homepage selection priority: session explicit choice, profile city, locally saved choice, previously granted approximate position, nearest active metro within 150 km, inventory fallback. Out-of-range visitors see nearby suggestions instead of an unrelated city.
Location/privacy behavior: No silent permission prompt; one reading on an explicit request or when already granted; coordinates rounded in memory, never persisted. Denial falls back.
Manual override behavior: Selection persists in localStorage, and Events near me clears it and requests location.
New-city activation behavior: A new registered slug plus an approved upcoming public event becomes active without frontend deployment. Admin must register the metro before event entry.
Empty-area behavior: Explanation, nearby active metros, city explorer, and submission action.
Canonical URLs: /events/:slug for registered metros, aliases redirect, UUID route remains event detail.

